## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of production-grade model serving, stateful components, and zero-downtime updates under streaming data.

## Key Concepts

- Embedding sharding and stateful serving
- Online updates without stale reads
- Atomic model version swaps and canary deployment
- Observability, SLAs, rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: versioned embedding cache lookup
const version = process.env.MODEL_VERSION || 'v1';
const embedCache = loadEmbeddingCache(version);

function predict(inputIds) {
  const emb = embedCache.lookup(inputIds);
  return model.apply(emb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test zero-downtime swap guarantees?
- What race conditions could arise and how would you mitigate them?

## Why This Is Asked
Explores multi-model inference orchestration under streaming load, with precise resource guarantees and safe upgrades.

## Key Concepts
- Per-model batching with isolation
- GPU memory quotas per model
- Streaming windowing and batch_timeout
- SLA-driven routing policy
- Canary rollouts and automatic rollback
- Tail latency monitoring and drift alerts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo config illustrating per-model batching and mem quotas
{
  "models": {
    "A": { "max_batch_size": 64, "batch_timeout_micros": 1000, "mem_quota_mb": 12288 },
    "B": { "max_batch_size": 128, "batch_timeout_micros": 1000, "mem_quota_mb": 8192 }
  },
  "routing": { "policy": "queue_depth" }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift detection and rollback criteria?
- What metrics and dashboards would you expose for operators?
